#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f7718f-e014-5232-acb1-6773ab79f61d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Defined Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2268decf-8057-5052-b22c-2d9db7931297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266451} {:answer/id #uuid "2b64e25b-869e-5a23-a2e6-e9bcb899719b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266528} {:answer/id #uuid "477faab4-1a81-5e30-989d-335ba513d783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266784} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a5dd31-4b38-5d68-841b-b0fe947ea52a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267616} {:answer/id #uuid "f1267f21-e92c-5711-a63a-3abce564f530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "477faab4-1a81-5e30-989d-335ba513d783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266784} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4dfa161-4dd2-52cf-bd87-7379b870a0f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c4cd592-9607-50f1-89a9-e38280b49bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-132527" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{D}y\\,dA,$ where $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2{y}^{2}\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+1\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2{y}^{2}\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+1\\}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}y\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}y\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[\\,x\\,]_{2{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}+1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y({y}^{2}+1-2{y}^{2})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ccbe70d-24f4-5e9c-8536-9ccab99f571b" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral When the Limits are Not Given"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28685095-749a-5991-9be2-402bf87a4783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{y/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475495} {:answer/id #uuid "b50cbc81-f2c6-5823-bd95-abc058fa081b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{\\sqrt{y}}{\\int }_{0}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475713} {:answer/id #uuid "c020b011-abec-5f74-a0d6-2e493cdf3a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}{\\int }_{2}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475735} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6d84dc-f6bf-5a95-aef6-2d114a0e442f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y}}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475751} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4f557a-0393-5b7c-9aa1-df8febbf44fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc4f557a-0393-5b7c-9aa1-df8febbf44fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475776} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cda2ff4-5dd7-546b-a1e2-111a796413b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "118a9fcd-c8c0-57b4-8e3a-7c92ff45ac8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40678" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y=2x$ and $y={x}^{2}$ above the line $y=2.$ What is ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA\\,$ expressed as a repeated integral?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/4e/4e58d7969f0b31206ae8c3385a857c0ad6cf8a42ee79909d51c3a6b58a090852.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=2x$ and $y={x}^{2}$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ y={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{y} & =\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y & =0 \\\\ y(y-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line $y=2,$ the $y$-limits are \n$2\\le y\\le 4.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/16/16944d6651297f1c13c39ddf3d9160d721f5f29bfa6b0acac0db46c88295964e.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ccbe70d-24f4-5e9c-8536-9ccab99f571b" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral When the Limits are Not Given"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dbf9137-cd18-5b00-8628-35682148d59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{3-{y}^{3}}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{3/2}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dx]dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482833} {:answer/id #uuid "27f8b3fc-0f1b-53d7-9969-248547e7b45b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3-{y}^{3}}[{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{\\sqrt[3]{3/2}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dx]dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482883} {:answer/id #uuid "5807c016-a68d-500a-bafd-bbe8e52e28c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{\\sqrt[3]{3/2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dx]dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482967} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7b1686-130b-5256-a8cd-ed668ee1fd00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{3/2}}[{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{3-{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dx]dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483032} {:answer/id #uuid "e13baa75-b4d0-5922-8e2d-cba1a3bda445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{3/2}}[{\\int }_{3-{y}^{3}}^{{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dx]dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d7b1686-130b-5256-a8cd-ed668ee1fd00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{3/2}}[{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{3-{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dx]dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483032} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7bebbb6-2b2e-5637-b8dd-0175f7869ed4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf43c215-ffc3-5823-9335-496b6c1fd83f" :question/math-academy-id "q-81301" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c3dbd6e26cb67b2f247387c30e03296f790c3f56c03779a7dda5ae5d0b081958.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines $x=3-{y}^{3},\\,$ $x={y}^{3},$ and $y=0,$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. \n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-{y}^{3} & ={y}^{3} \\\\ 2{y}^{3} & =3 \\\\ {y}^{3} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{3}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{3}{2}}.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/36/366146b42d476b8d2a467e607a3bba1ef65ddc8a344b3f0e17ee4652ccc0463a.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{3}{2}},\\,{y}^{3}\\le x\\le 3-{y}^{3}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{3/2}}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{3-{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{3/2}}[{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{3-{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdce40e5-8ffe-52cb-8a8e-ac8eaea982f0" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral Defined Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "446d2ae8-dc82-50e7-896b-5418a7d5cfcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482930} {:answer/id #uuid "bb439f1a-410c-5eb8-8f44-0f5d3790b885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483127} {:answer/id #uuid "beec0d21-4472-5b7e-8a67-4ff29eca2542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483132} {:answer/id #uuid "d948eeb8-aa2f-59a3-84a4-d8a991007f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483178} {:answer/id #uuid "ef86a85c-17ca-562f-9487-9b3559e88804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb439f1a-410c-5eb8-8f44-0f5d3790b885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483127} :answer-field/id #uuid "899b1e4d-10a7-5a27-99db-9badc378d5e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2f72ec4-b491-5de0-a559-269634816f5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81312" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{{y}^{2}}(y-1)\\,dx\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{{y}^{2}}(y-1)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-1)[{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-1)\\,[x]_{{y}^{3}}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-1)({y}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{y}^{4}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{y}^{4}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={[-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdce40e5-8ffe-52cb-8a8e-ac8eaea982f0" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral Defined Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054cfdb8-9523-5fd3-8ee5-f3584ca875a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348495} {:answer/id #uuid "1a58f340-5f07-524b-9972-7aec7a072fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348668} {:answer/id #uuid "413f25e1-e820-5b99-b415-72140d39e76a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349040} {:answer/id #uuid "630cd449-0bac-53d3-aade-e06771d4eb3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349353} {:answer/id #uuid "df055118-5d65-5cb6-afdd-037e1bc8f8e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a58f340-5f07-524b-9972-7aec7a072fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348668} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb3e7c8f-9e68-503e-917d-bfcf6dae85d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f40afbe3-1000-5dc9-b06f-6a8edbf20249" :question/math-academy-id "q-81315" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3\\pi /2}}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dy.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3\\pi /2}}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}[x]_{0}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}(y-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3\\pi /2}}y\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3\\pi /2}}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}\\,dy & ={[\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3\\pi /2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
